fixes.note:
Extracted the whole screen *shell* into `src/components/cart/use-cart-screen.ts` (328 lines) and merged the two `z-Complete.tsx` copies into `src/components/cart/z-Complete.tsx`.

What is now single-source (was duplicated verbatim in both `page.tsx`):
- mode-filtered `drafts`/`normalDrafts`/`tabs` memos (incl. the STORED_FLAG ordering);
- the `creating` ref guard + "the screen always has a cart" effect with `startError`/`retryStart`;
- the `restoring` latch and its 1000 ms safety net, driven by one `restore` object (`onStart`/`onEnd`/`onRestored`) both screens hand to `Complete`;
- the `?draft=` repair (`active = normalDrafts.find(...) ?? normalDrafts[0]`);
- the `findLineIssues`/`hasHardIssue` memo (and the `listing.get.changes` subscription that feeds it);
- the tab-switch stage reset + deferred search-focus bump;
- the Ctrl/Cmd+Arrow tab walker, F1/F2/F12 dispatch (F1/F2 are now documented props, F12/Escape are fixed);
- `storeCart`, `openDraft` (parked tab re-expansion), `lines`/`extras`/`setLines`/`setExtras`, `submitting`, `complete`, `startError`, `focusSearch`.

Divergence resolved:
- Restock now uses `cart.tabs` + `cart.openDraft`, so a parked (`STORED_FLAG`) purchase tab is restorable by click exactly as on Pos.
- Restock's F2 no longer lives in `Draft/index.tsx`; it is the page's `onF2` and means the same thing as on Pos ("settle": open the payment stage / focus the payment rows), so one component owns every shortcut.
- The one remaining deliberate difference is the `area` ("which panel owns the selection") model, which only Pos needs because both of its grids are on screen at once — documented in `Pos/page.tsx`.

Result: `git diff --stat` = −974/+415 (plus the two new shared files); `Pos/page.tsx` 414→209, `Restock/page.tsx` 393→243, the two `z-Complete.tsx` (378) → one (203). Both pages now contain zero `useEffect`, zero creation `useRef`, zero URL-writing code.

Remaining (why partial, not fixed): the `<Draft>`/`<Bottom>` render trees stay per screen, so `wc -l` is 452 combined, not the report's <120. Those trees are not copies — Pos's bottom is a settle strip with five hand-off tokens + park, Restock's is a stage stepper with the credit dialog — and forcing them behind one slot-based component would add ~15 props without deleting per-screen knowledge. The remaining duplicated *text* is the 6-line total/grand/change formula in each page (identical math, different extra `creditGrand`).

Follow-up for the next auditor: a render test mounting both pages through the shared hook (see the `no-component-render-tests` report) is now cheap because the hook is the seam; the only remaining keyboard asymmetry to watch is Restock having no park/store button in its bottom panel.
